               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_90633b27">In 2<rend xml:id="idm31" rend="sup">o</rend>; 2 folded bifolios, trimmed; fols. 1v–2r contains the text for<rend xml:id="idm32" fontstyle="italic"> Führe uns nicht in Versuchung</rend> ('Ich danke dir, mein Vater in der Höhe'); written in black ink. The source has 10 stanzas rather than the 9 which the printed edition has. The source contains also other texts by Münter and is presumably his autograph.</physMedium>
